# The Challenge of Advocacy: The Different Voices of Helen Keller and Burton Blatt.

**Authors:** Smith, J. David

## Abstract
Comparison of the different advocacy roles of Helen Keller and Burton Blatt finds that Helen Keller's role supports the belief in miracles resulting from unconditional and sustained commitments, whereas Burton Blatt's role illustrates the value of a commitment to human rights and human dignity regardless of any expectation of productivity or independence. (DB)

